{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>We all.</b> At the end they will recognize the truth, and behold it is joined with נָגוּעַ (stricken) and מֻכֵּה אֱלֹהִים, and like it: אָךְ שֶׁקֶר נָחֲלוּ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ (Jeremiah 16:19)." "<b>Has encountered.</b> From the root of וַיִּפְגַּע בַּמָּקוֹם (Genesis 28:11)." "<b>עָוֹן.</b> In this place it means punishment, like אִם־יִקְרְךָ עָוֹן (1 Samuel 28:10), כִּי לֹא־שָׁלֵם עֲוֺן הָאֱמֹרִי (Genesis 15:16), וַיִּגְדַּל עָוֺן בַּת־עַמִּי (Lamentations 4:6). And some say it is from the root of וְאַל־תְּפַגַּע בִּי (Jeremiah 7:16), and the meaning of עָוֹן כֻּלָּנוּ would then be according to its plain sense, and the sense is that he encounters for the sake of there being peace in the world, like the sense of וְדִרְשׁוּ אֶת־שְׁלוֹם הָעִיר [Jeremiah 29:7]; therefore the word עָוֹן is placed harshly with הִפְגִּיעַ in him:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {0 "Resolved the unattributed verse citation to Jeremiah 16:19 based on the phrase quoted."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:24.434098912Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}